    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but when you look at the actual outcomes, like in recent years, it almost feels like the UN lacks any real authority if a major power decides to ignore it. do historians think the institution is actually still a legitimate way to govern international relations, or is the idea of a \"rules-based order\" just a convenient narrative that's losing its touch with reality?",
