      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Many contemporary political realists argue that the \"rules-based order\" is indeed in decline because powerful states prioritize national interest (power politics) over institutional commitment. However, a more nuanced view is that the UN, though often limited, still provides the *only* universally accepted forum for state-to-state dialogue, making it a necessary, if often politically constrained, part of the global system.",
      "source": "target",
